From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000078 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 16:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] r25-0078: replay ordered path runs across live text barriers

Consume the holder-owned RenderProgram v2 for the first mixed-command shape:
exact path and text streams. One non-path object must not force every tile back
through a multi-million-object canonical holder walk.

Build a compact segment table while the legacy path display list is compiled:
consecutive eligible paths become PathRun segments and text commands become
ordered passthrough barriers. Compile and validate the complete display list
before drawing. Replay every segment in painter order, resolve text by live
holder index rather than a cached pointer, and reset PDFium's clip state at
each acceleration boundary.

The policy remains fail closed. Image, Form, shading, unsupported commands,
object-kind mismatches, unsupported path paint, and segment-budget overflow
return before accelerated drawing. Segment storage has a hard one-million-entry
ceiling. No Kotlin classification, JNI API, UI-thread work, scheduler, or
document-specific rule is added.

Telemetry reports parser text counts, segment counts, and passthrough counts so
Q16-like holders can be distinguished from canonical fallback.
---
